    <section
      class="feature-grid"
      id="features"
      aria-label="Markly features"
    >
      <article class="feature-card wide reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Library & Folders</p>

        <h3>Give every saved link a place to belong</h3>

        <p>
          Build a structured bookmark library using folders that you can create,
          customize, reorder, search, and manage. Markly keeps an Inbox ready for
          new saves while giving you the freedom to create dedicated spaces for
          projects, research, inspiration, shopping, articles, references, or
          anything else you collect online.
        </p>

        <div class="chip-row">
          <span>Folders</span>
          <span>Inbox</span>
          <span>Search</span>
          <span>Reordering</span>
          <span>Favorites</span>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Rich Bookmarks</p>

        <h3>Save more than just a URL</h3>

        <p>
          Every bookmark can carry a title, description, link, tags, notes,
          website imagery, folder placement, favorite state, pinned state, and
          archive state so the reason you saved something does not disappear
          with time.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Pin Collections</p>

        <h3>Keep important links one tap away</h3>

        <p>
          Pin your most useful bookmarks and group them into custom collections.
          Give each collection its own name, icon, notes, and bookmark set to
          build quick-access spaces for the links you return to most.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Search, Filter & Sort</p>

        <h3>Find the thing you saved six weeks ago</h3>

        <p>
          Search across bookmark titles, descriptions, tags, notes, and links,
          then narrow your library with quick filters and sorting controls.
          Markly is built for finding things again, not simply collecting them.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Notes</p>

        <h3>Keep the context that made a link worth saving</h3>

        <p>
          Add thoughts, takeaways, reminders, quotes, research notes, or anything
          else you want attached to a saved link. A bookmark can hold multiple
          saved notes so your relationship with a resource can grow over time.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="feature-card wide reveal">
        <p class="card-kicker">Reader Mode</p>

        <h3>Turn saved articles into a calmer reading experience</h3>

        <p>
          Open supported links inside Markly's dedicated Reader. Markly extracts
          the readable article content, removes surrounding page clutter, keeps
          track of your reading progress, surfaces article metadata, and lets you
          adjust text size without losing access to the original webpage.
        </p>

        <div class="reader-preview">
          <div class="reader-preview-top">
            <span>Reader Progress</span>
            <strong>68%</strong>
          </div>

          <div class="reader-bar">
            <span></span>
          </div>

          <div class="reader-meta">
            <span>12 min read</span>
            <span>Comfortable text</span>
            <span>Original available</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="spotlight reveal">
      <div class="spotlight-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Save From Anywhere</p>

        <h2>Send a link straight to Markly from the iOS share sheet</h2>

        <p>
          Markly includes its own share extension, so you do not have to stop
          what you are doing just to organize something worth keeping. Share a
          webpage to Markly, review its title, description, URL and tags, choose
          the destination folder, and save it directly into your library.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="share-demo" aria-label="Markly share preview">
        <span class="share-pill">Save to Markly</span>

        <h4>Worth keeping?</h4>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Title</span>
          <strong>Already filled in</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Folder</span>
          <strong>Choose where it belongs</strong>
        </div>

        <div class="share-row">
          <span>Tags</span>
          <strong>Add context now</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="details-section reveal">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Everything Else</p>

        <h2>Open each part of the Markly experience</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="details-list">
        <details open>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Bookmark Details & Web Preview</b>
              <small>See the link, its context, and the page itself</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Open any bookmark to view its folder, tags, description, saved link,
            and notes from one dedicated detail page. Switch to Preview to load
            the webpage directly inside Markly, or open it in the system browser
            whenever you want the original experience.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Favorites, Pins & Archive</b>
              <small>Different ways to organize what matters right now</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Favorite the links you care about most, pin the ones that deserve
            quick access, place pinned bookmarks into dedicated collections, or
            archive links you want to keep without leaving them in your active
            workflow.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Activity</b>
              <small>See the shape of your Markly library as it grows</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            The Activity page brings together library statistics and recent
            bookmark, folder, and collection activity. See how many bookmarks,
            folders, and collections you have and revisit the things that were
            recently created or updated.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Cloud Sync</b>
              <small>Keep your library available across your devices</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Sign in with Apple and use Markly's CloudKit-backed sync system to
            keep supported bookmark data connected across your devices. Saved
            links, folders, tags, notes, favorites, archive state, and link
            metadata can move with your Markly library instead of being trapped
            on one device.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Import Bookmarks</b>
              <small>Bring an existing collection into Markly</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Import bookmarks from supported JSON, CSV, and Markdown files.
            Choose whether to preserve the original folder information or direct
            imported bookmarks into a specific Markly folder, with imported and
            skipped counts shown as the process completes.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Export & Backups</b>
              <small>Your bookmark library does not have to stay locked in</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Export your entire library, a single folder, your favorites, or your
            archived bookmarks. Markly can generate JSON backups, readable
            Markdown exports, or CSV files for spreadsheets and other tools,
            then hand the resulting file back to the system share sheet.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>
            <span>
              <b>Built-In Support</b>
              <small>Report problems and ideas without leaving the app</small>
            </span>
          </summary>

          <p>
            Markly includes dedicated forms for bug reports, feature requests,
            and beta feedback, plus a Submitted area where reports sent from the
            device can be reviewed later. Support is part of the app experience
            rather than something hidden somewhere else.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="community-banner reveal">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Built for Collectors of the Web</p>

        <h2>The internet is huge. Your saved corner of it does not have to be.</h2>

        <p>
          Markly is built for people who constantly find things worth returning
          to: articles, tools, references, inspiration, research, resources,
          products, guides, ideas, and everything in between. Save freely, then
          give those discoveries enough structure that they are useful again
          later.
        </p>
      </div>

      <a class="primary-button raised-button" href="/github">
        Join the Community
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="cta-section reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Explore Markly</p>

      <h2>Your bookmarks deserve better than becoming a forgotten pile of links.</h2>

      <p>
        Learn more about Markly, report a problem, share an idea, or reach out
        directly through Voxiverse Support.
      </p>

      <div class="cta-grid">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/asteriasmoons/Markly/issues"
          class="cta-card"
        >
          <span class="cta-kicker">Report an Issue</span>

          <h2>Markly Bug Reports</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Open Reports</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/github" class="cta-card">
          <span class="cta-kicker">Ideas & Discussions</span>

          <h2>Voxiverse on GitHub</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Open GitHub</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/contact" class="cta-card">
          <span class="cta-kicker">Need Help?</span>

          <h2>Contact Support</h2>

          <span class="cta-button">Get Support</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<script>
  const revealItems = document.querySelectorAll(".reveal");

  const revealObserver = new IntersectionObserver(
    (entries) => {
      entries.forEach((entry) => {
        if (entry.isIntersecting) {
          entry.target.classList.add("is-visible");
          revealObserver.unobserve(entry.target);
        }
      });
    },
    { threshold: 0.12 }
  );

  revealItems.forEach((item) => revealObserver.observe(item));

  document
    .querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-markly-gallery]")
    .forEach((gallery) => {
      const track =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-track]");

      const slides = Array.from(
        gallery.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".gallery-slide")
      );

      const previousButton =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
          "[data-gallery-previous]"
        );

      const nextButton =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
          "[data-gallery-next]"
        );

      const count =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-count]");

      const progress =
        gallery.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gallery-progress]");

      if (
        !track ||
        !slides.length ||
        !previousButton ||
        !nextButton
      ) {
        return;
      }

      let currentIndex = 0;
      let autoplay: number | undefined;
      let dragStartX = 0;

      const updateGallery = () => {
        track.style.transform =
          `translateX(-${currentIndex * 100}%)`;

        slides.forEach((slide, index) => {
          slide.classList.toggle(
            "is-active",
            index === currentIndex
          );
        });

        if (count) {
          count.textContent =
            `${currentIndex + 1} / ${slides.length}`;
        }

        if (progress) {
          progress.style.width =
            `${((currentIndex + 1) / slides.length) * 100}%`;
        }
      };

      const showSlide = (index: number) => {
        currentIndex =
          (index + slides.length) % slides.length;

        updateGallery();
      };

      const startAutoplay = () => {
        window.clearInterval(autoplay);

        autoplay = window.setInterval(
          () => showSlide(currentIndex + 1),
          4200
        );
      };

      const stopAutoplay = () => {
        window.clearInterval(autoplay);
      };

      nextButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        showSlide(currentIndex + 1);
        startAutoplay();
      });

      previousButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
        showSlide(currentIndex - 1);
        startAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener("pointerdown", (event) => {
        dragStartX = event.clientX;
        stopAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener("pointerup", (event) => {
        const deltaX = event.clientX - dragStartX;

        if (Math.abs(deltaX) > 40) {
          showSlide(
            currentIndex + (deltaX < 0 ? 1 : -1)
          );
        }

        startAutoplay();
      });

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "mouseenter",
        stopAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "mouseleave",
        startAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "focusin",
        stopAutoplay
      );

      gallery.addEventListener(
        "focusout",
        startAutoplay
      );

      window.addEventListener(
        "resize",
        updateGallery
      );

      updateGallery();
      startAutoplay();
    });
</script>

<style>
  .markly-page {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 1rem 0 5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hero {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(0, 1.2fr)
      minmax(310px, 0.8fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3rem;
    min-height: 620px;
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }

  .hero-copy,
  .hero-showcase {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6.5rem);
    line-height: 0.96;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .card-kicker,
  .mini-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .hero-text,
  .intro-section p,
  .spotlight p,
  .community-banner p,
  .cta-section > p {
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: 1.06rem;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .primary-button,
  .secondary-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 50px;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.3rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--color-bg);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .primary-button {
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .secondary-button {
    background: var(--surface-raised) !important;
    color: var(--color-text) !important;
  }

  .primary-button:hover,
  .secondary-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .hero-showcase {
    min-height: 410px;
  }

  .showcase-card,
  .floating-card,
  .feature-card,
  .share-demo,
  .details-list details,
  .community-banner,
  .cta-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--surface-standard);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow-soft);
  }

  .main-card {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 55px 20px 55px 30px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 2rem;
    border-radius: 30px;
    transform: rotate(2deg);
  }

  .main-card h4 {
    max-width: 420px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .progress-line {
    height: 10px;
    margin: 1.75rem 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .progress-line span {
    display: block;
    width: 72%;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: inherit;
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
    animation: pulse-width 3s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  .showcase-stats {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .showcase-stats b {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .floating-card {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 3;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    border-radius: 18px;
    animation: float 5s ease-in-out infinite;
  }

  .floating-card span {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .floating-card strong {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .floating-card-one {
    top: 0;
    right: 0;
  }

  .floating-card-two {
    bottom: 8px;
    left: 0;
    animation-delay: -2.4s;
  }

  @media (min-width: 901px) {
    :global(.content:has(.markly-page)) {
      max-width: 1280px;
      padding-inline: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 3rem);
    }

    .hero {
      grid-template-columns:
        minmax(0, 1fr)
        minmax(340px, 380px);
      gap: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 4rem);
      min-height: 610px;
      padding: 2.15rem 0 2.65rem;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      max-width: 840px;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      font-size: 4.15rem;
      line-height: 1;
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    .hero-text {
      max-width: 660px;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .hero-actions {
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }

    .hero-showcase {
      align-self: center;
      justify-self: end;
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 380px;
      min-height: 430px;
    }

    .main-card {
      inset: 58px 16px 104px 16px;
      padding: 1.45rem;
      border-radius: 26px;
      transform: none;
    }

    .main-card h4 {
      max-width: 320px;
      font-size: 2.35rem;
    }

    .progress-line {
      margin: 1.2rem 0;
    }

    .showcase-stats {
      gap: 0.65rem 0.9rem;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }

    .floating-card-one {
      top: 0;
      right: 0;
      max-width: 282px;
    }

    .floating-card-two {
      bottom: 16px;
      left: 0;
      max-width: 292px;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 901px) and (max-width: 1160px) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns:
        minmax(0, 1fr)
        minmax(320px, 340px);
      gap: 2rem;
    }

    .hero h1 {
      font-size: 3.7rem;
    }

    .main-card h4 {
      font-size: 2.1rem;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1400px) {
    .hero h1 {
      font-size: 4.75rem;
    }
  }

  .intro-section {
    max-width: 850px;
    padding: 4rem 0 2rem;
  }

  .intro-section h2,
  .gallery-heading h2,
  .spotlight h2,
  .details-section h2,
  .community-banner h2,
  .cta-section h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .markly-gallery-section {
    position: relative;
    padding: 2rem 0 3.25rem;
  }

  .gallery-heading {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .markly-gallery {
    position: relative;
    width: min(100%, 430px);
    margin: 0 auto;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: 1rem 0 2.75rem;
    touch-action: pan-y;
  }

  .gallery-track-container {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: 32px;
  }

  .gallery-track {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    will-change: transform;
    transition:
      transform 0.62s
      cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1);
  }

  .gallery-slide {
